kept.suggested_fix:
Refuse to swallow an in-flight cancellation of this task. `Task.cancelling()` is still non-zero after a CancelledError has been delivered and swallowed (only `TaskGroup.__aexit__` calls `uncancel()`), so a two-line guard at the top of the `except PoisonedSessionError` and `except Exception` arms covers every source of an abort and needs nothing from the drivers:
            if (t := asyncio.current_task()) is not None and t.cancelling():
                raise      # the gate task group is tearing this session down
